WEBVTT

00:02.014 --> 00:03.390
<i>Previously on</i> Lost:

00:03.473 --> 00:07.342
This is not your island.
This is our island.

00:07.436 --> 00:12.180
<i>They've attacked us</i>, <i>sabotaged us</i>,
<i>abducted us</i>, <i>murdered us.</i>

00:12.274 --> 00:16.142
<i>We're not the only people</i>
<i>on this island</i>, <i>and we all know it.</i>

00:16.236 --> 00:19.031
<i>They came the first night</i>,
<i>took three of us.</i>

00:19.114 --> 00:22.451
<i>Then they came back</i>
<i>and took nine more.</i>

00:22.534 --> 00:25.412
<i>They're smart and they're animals.</i>

00:25.495 --> 00:27.654
You're coming with us.

01:35.983 --> 01:39.601
I burnt my hand. And my muffins.

01:41.780 --> 01:45.993
- Still hasn't fixed your plumbing yet?
- It's a work in progress.

01:47.536 --> 01:50.163
It's not even literature.
It's popcorn.

01:50.247 --> 01:52.916
Why isn't it literature, Adam?
I'm dying to know.

01:53.000 --> 01:57.379
There's no metaphor. It's religious
hokum-pokum. It's science fiction.

01:57.462 --> 02:00.257
- Now I know why Ben isn't here.
- Excuse me?

02:00.340 --> 02:02.634
I know the host
picks the book, but, Julie,

02:02.718 --> 02:05.293
he wouldn't read this
in the damned bathroom.

02:05.387 --> 02:10.298
Well, Adam, I am the host,
and I do pick the book.

02:10.392 --> 02:13.103
And this is my favourite book,

02:13.186 --> 02:18.066
so I am absolutely thrilled
that you can't stand it.

02:18.150 --> 02:22.279
Silly me for sinking so low as to select
something that Ben wouldn't like.

02:22.362 --> 02:26.533
Here I am thinking that freewill
still actually exists on...

02:28.410 --> 02:31.330
- Whoa.
- The doorway. Get under the doorway.

03:25.842 --> 03:26.875
Goodwin.

03:29.554 --> 03:32.557
- You see where the tail landed?
- Probably in the water.

03:32.641 --> 03:36.144
You can make that shore in an hour.
Ethan, get up to that fuselage.

03:36.228 --> 03:38.636
There may actually be survivors.

03:38.730 --> 03:41.608
And you're one of 'em.
A passenger. You're in shock.

03:41.692 --> 03:44.861
Come up with a story if they ask.
Stay quiet if they don't.

03:44.945 --> 03:46.989
Listen. Learn. Don't get involved.

03:47.072 --> 03:49.397
I want lists in three days. Go.

03:59.001 --> 04:02.004
So, I guess I'm out of the book club.

06:44.207 --> 06:45.751
Hey!

06:47.085 --> 06:48.587
Kate!

06:49.630 --> 06:52.090
Can you hear me?

06:53.634 --> 06:55.844
Kate!

07:06.897 --> 07:09.816
Rise and shine, Kate.

07:13.862 --> 07:15.061
Where am I?

07:15.155 --> 07:18.273
You don't really think
I'm going to answer that, do you?

07:19.868 --> 07:23.319
- Where are Sawyer and Jack?
- I'll tell you what.

07:23.413 --> 07:27.417
Why don't you just take a nice
hot shower, wake yourself up,

07:27.501 --> 07:30.337
wash the day off you and start fresh?

07:30.420 --> 07:33.173
Here's a nice clean towel,
shampoo, soap...

07:33.256 --> 07:35.582
I'm not showering in front of you.

07:37.928 --> 07:40.639
Kate, you're not my type.

08:32.649 --> 08:33.817
Hey.

08:38.196 --> 08:40.949
Where are we?

08:42.534 --> 08:45.245
Who the hell are you?

08:47.998 --> 08:49.989
You ain't gonna talk to me?

08:51.001 --> 08:54.755
What, you got
more important things to do?

09:28.372 --> 09:29.790
<i>Warning.</i>

09:37.798 --> 09:39.132
<i>Warning.</i>

09:42.135 --> 09:44.096
I wouldn't do that.

09:44.179 --> 09:46.473
If I want your advice, I'll ask for it.

09:52.521 --> 09:54.262
Son of a bitch!

09:55.732 --> 09:57.474
Told you.

10:23.010 --> 10:24.469
Stop that.

10:34.146 --> 10:35.314
Hi, Jack.

10:37.316 --> 10:39.307
I'm Juliet.

10:49.328 --> 10:53.113
Hi. I'm Jack Shephard.
I'm here for the...

10:53.206 --> 10:56.126
Where's your lawyer?

11:04.509 --> 11:07.346
You look pretty.

11:07.429 --> 11:09.421
Where's your lawyer?

11:13.352 --> 11:15.343
I fired him.

11:17.981 --> 11:19.973
Sarah...

11:22.110 --> 11:27.188
I'm sorry for pushing us to this place.

11:27.282 --> 11:29.660
I know that I...

11:33.705 --> 11:35.864
Excuse me. I'm sorry.

11:37.000 --> 11:38.377
Yeah?

11:41.088 --> 11:43.757
No, not yet. He just got here.

11:45.884 --> 11:48.209
I'll call you when I get out.

11:55.268 --> 11:58.522
- I'm gonna say this as simply as I can.
- What's his name?

11:58.605 --> 12:00.482
- Stop it.
- I'm not gonna stop it.

12:00.565 --> 12:02.891
I'm gonna keep asking you
until you tell me.

12:02.985 --> 12:06.186
- I don't ask you what you do...
- Just tell me what his name is.

12:06.279 --> 12:09.241
I wanna know who he is.

12:10.242 --> 12:13.829
Look, you can have everything,
the cars, the house, I don't care.

12:13.912 --> 12:17.749
I just... I just wanna know

12:17.833 --> 12:23.255
the name of the man
that is with my wife.

12:43.734 --> 12:45.944
Jack?

12:47.321 --> 12:50.490
Can you hear me in there?

12:53.869 --> 12:56.705
- Is that a yes?
- Where are my friends?

12:56.788 --> 12:58.373
Come down from the table.

12:58.457 --> 13:01.335
You want me to come down,
come in here and get me down.

13:01.418 --> 13:05.589
- If you wanna talk, I'm happy to.
- Tell me where my friends are!

13:06.548 --> 13:09.217
I will if you let go of the chain.

13:10.886 --> 13:14.003
Do you think I'm stupid?

13:16.016 --> 13:19.936
I don't think you're stupid, Jack.

13:20.020 --> 13:22.981
I think you're stubborn.

13:52.469 --> 13:54.461
Hey!

13:55.305 --> 13:57.766
Where are my clothes?

14:26.837 --> 14:30.257
Come on, Kate. He's waiting.

15:40.494 --> 15:44.279
Sorry. I'm going to have to ask you
to put those on, Kate.

15:44.373 --> 15:46.614
And if I don't?

15:47.751 --> 15:50.076
Then you don't get any coffee.

16:03.892 --> 16:05.884
A little tighter.

16:08.063 --> 16:10.055
Please?

16:19.700 --> 16:23.318
What did you do with Sawyer and Jack?

16:23.412 --> 16:25.403
Now, why Sawyer?

16:26.373 --> 16:29.908
- Why Sawyer what?
- He's the first one you asked about.

16:30.002 --> 16:33.036
"What did you do with Sawyer and Jack"?

16:35.632 --> 16:38.666
- You don't know me.
- Of course I don't.

16:41.221 --> 16:45.142
- I want my clothes back.
- We burned them.

16:46.852 --> 16:49.146
Why did you bring me here?

16:49.229 --> 16:52.149
Why did you make me put on this dress?

16:52.232 --> 16:54.224
Why are you feeding me breakfast?

16:57.195 --> 17:00.949
I brought you here so you'd look out
at the water and feel comforted,

17:01.033 --> 17:05.912
comforted that your friends
were looking out at the same ocean.

17:05.996 --> 17:09.197
I gave you the dress
so you'd feel like a lady.

17:10.292 --> 17:13.493
And I wanted you to eat your food
with a real live fork

17:13.587 --> 17:15.912
and feel civilised.

17:18.300 --> 17:23.378
I did all those things so that you'd
have something nice to hold onto.

17:24.765 --> 17:27.882
Because, Kate,

17:27.976 --> 17:32.272
the next two weeks
are going to be very unpleasant.

17:44.409 --> 17:49.539
Yeah, hi. I met a woman
on the train, Sarah,

17:49.623 --> 17:53.710
and she dropped her cell phone
and I don't even know her last name,

17:53.794 --> 17:58.173
but your number was in her phone,
so I was just wondering...

17:58.256 --> 18:00.415
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. Forget it.

18:00.509 --> 18:03.220
- Hey.
- Just give me a minute, Dad.

18:05.973 --> 18:08.048
I asked you to give me a minute here.

18:08.141 --> 18:13.897
What's this? Why are you dialling
all the numbers on Sarah's cell phone?

18:13.981 --> 18:18.558
- Because one of them is him.
- You gotta stop this, Jack. It's over.

18:18.652 --> 18:21.530
Not until I know his name,

18:21.613 --> 18:24.700
where he works, where he lives,
when they first kissed.

18:24.783 --> 18:27.703
I wanna know what it is about him.

18:36.795 --> 18:39.339
Why is Sarah calling you, Dad?

18:40.757 --> 18:43.552
I think it's time that you let this go.

18:43.635 --> 18:47.504
- Why is she calling you?
- Because she was afraid for you.

18:47.597 --> 18:50.799
I wanna know exactly
why the hell she was calling.

18:50.892 --> 18:53.270
You were slipping, losing your grip.

18:53.353 --> 18:58.066
- My grip is not the problem here.
- Which is exactly what's happening.

18:58.150 --> 19:00.986
I think I know something
about being obsessive.

19:01.069 --> 19:06.491
No. Being a drunk is not obsessive.

19:19.212 --> 19:21.287
Let it go, Jack.

19:54.998 --> 19:56.990
What?

19:58.835 --> 20:02.454
If you're trying to talk to me,
I can't hear you.

20:02.547 --> 20:05.634
<i>Let it go</i>, <i>Jack.</i>

20:09.179 --> 20:12.015
I know you're hungry.
I brought this for you.

20:14.059 --> 20:15.967
This is how it will work.

20:16.061 --> 20:20.472
You sit there, across from the door,
back against the wall.

20:20.565 --> 20:24.069
I open the door and leave the tray.

20:24.152 --> 20:26.311
Can I trust you to do that, Jack?

20:29.366 --> 20:32.369
- I don't want your food.
- It's a delicious sandwich.

20:32.452 --> 20:36.915
Tell the guy who's trying to talk to me
through that intercom he can give it up!

20:38.375 --> 20:42.546
Maybe you're hungrier than you think.
That intercom hasn't worked in years.

20:44.381 --> 20:47.665
What's that for?
The button, what's it for?

20:48.510 --> 20:52.431
- It's for emergencies.
- Who's watching me?

20:53.807 --> 20:57.092
Are you going to sit against the wall
so I can open the door?

20:57.185 --> 21:00.105
It's just off the frying pan.

21:00.188 --> 21:02.180
You can have it.

21:08.447 --> 21:12.826
What do you do, Jack?
What's your profession?

21:12.909 --> 21:15.402
I'm a repo man.

21:15.495 --> 21:18.863
You know, when people don't pay
their bills, I go in for the bank

21:18.957 --> 21:21.418
and I collect their possessions.

21:21.501 --> 21:24.129
I'm a people person,
so I really love it.

21:24.212 --> 21:26.089
Are you married?

21:26.173 --> 21:30.260
No. I never saw the point.

21:30.344 --> 21:32.669
What about you?

21:32.763 --> 21:36.975
What's your job,
besides making sandwiches?

21:37.059 --> 21:40.812
I didn't make it.
I just put the toothpicks in.

21:45.692 --> 21:49.821
When your plane crashed,
where were you flying from?

21:58.330 --> 21:59.873
Sydney.

22:00.332 --> 22:02.960
What were you doing there?

22:03.043 --> 22:05.368
I was bringing my father home.

22:05.462 --> 22:10.342
- Why go all the way to Australia to...
- Because he was dead.

22:12.052 --> 22:14.262
I'm sorry.

22:15.180 --> 22:18.767
Yeah, I'm sure you are.

22:18.850 --> 22:21.061
Thanks.

22:27.693 --> 22:31.196
You can trust me, Jack.

22:31.279 --> 22:34.950
I'm not gonna hurt you.

22:42.791 --> 22:46.409
What the hell is going on here?

23:12.070 --> 23:13.572
Hey!

23:16.241 --> 23:19.442
Hey, how long would it take
to get to your camp?

23:19.536 --> 23:22.289
What, you're talking to me now, Chachi?

23:23.790 --> 23:26.251
From where they got you,
how long a walk was it?

23:26.335 --> 23:28.410
Day? Two days?

23:28.503 --> 23:31.256
Hey, what are the people like,
from your plane?

23:31.340 --> 23:33.884
They're just awesome.

23:33.967 --> 23:37.471
Last one of you boys came for a visit
got tortured by our Iraqi.

23:37.554 --> 23:40.046
He tortured me, too.

23:40.140 --> 23:43.508
But, hell, you don't know any better.

23:47.064 --> 23:48.096
<i>Subject escape.</i>

23:48.190 --> 23:49.222
- Hey
- Whoa.

23:49.316 --> 23:51.610
<i>Subject escape. Subject escape.</i>

23:51.693 --> 23:55.280
Hey, how'd you get out of there?

23:58.116 --> 23:59.399
- Run that way.
- Hold on.

23:59.493 --> 24:01.484
You run that way.

24:17.719 --> 24:19.711
Hey.

24:51.878 --> 24:54.881
Say it. Say it, Karl.

24:56.591 --> 24:59.261
I'm... sorry...

25:01.054 --> 25:05.434
...sorry I involved you
in my breakout attempt.

25:34.671 --> 25:37.163
The drugs we gave you
when we brought you here

25:37.257 --> 25:40.510
have a fairly serious side effect:
dehydration.

25:40.594 --> 25:43.221
Your head is probably sore,
your throat is raw,

25:43.305 --> 25:45.682
and if you don't eat or drink
something soon,

25:45.766 --> 25:47.924
you're going to start hallucinating.

25:51.355 --> 25:53.513
So you're a doctor, huh?

25:54.691 --> 25:58.445
No. I'm a repo woman.

26:02.157 --> 26:05.942
No strings attached.
You don't have to answer any questions.

26:06.036 --> 26:07.913
You don't have to do anything

26:07.996 --> 26:10.572
but sit with your back
up against the far wall,

26:10.666 --> 26:13.669
let me open that door,
put the plate down and leave.

26:16.964 --> 26:19.039
I know it feels like you're giving up,

26:19.132 --> 26:23.001
like you're losing
if you do anything that I ask you to,

26:23.095 --> 26:25.336
but you're not.

26:25.430 --> 26:27.505
You need to eat.

26:31.395 --> 26:33.470
What do you say?

27:09.016 --> 27:11.007
Thank you, Jack.

27:17.858 --> 27:22.237
Let's take out the epidural catheter
and get him started on a PCA.

27:23.196 --> 27:25.490
Excuse me for just a second.

27:25.574 --> 27:28.744
You sure he's ready
to self-administer his pain meds?

27:28.827 --> 27:30.819
Hello?

27:40.005 --> 27:41.996
Dr Shephard?

27:44.468 --> 27:46.793
Yeah. Bye.

28:26.927 --> 28:28.752
- Jack?
- Give me your cell phone.

28:28.845 --> 28:31.004
- What? What?
- I wanna see it. Now.

28:31.098 --> 28:35.894
Look where you are, Jack.
Just look around you. Please.

28:36.645 --> 28:38.271
- OK?
- Give me the phone.

28:38.355 --> 28:40.930
This is not the place for this.

28:41.024 --> 28:44.976
You must be Jack.
Why don't you grab a chair, join us?

28:51.952 --> 28:54.527
You... you know me?

28:54.621 --> 28:57.582
Yes. Your father's told us
all about you.

28:57.666 --> 29:01.253
What's he told you about me?
What'd you tell them about me, Dad?

29:01.336 --> 29:05.173
That your son never really had it?
Not like the old man.

29:06.425 --> 29:11.138
I didn't have the will to make it work?
My life? My job?

29:11.221 --> 29:16.018
My marriage? What'd you tell them
about my marriage, Dad?

29:16.810 --> 29:19.354
You know how he manages his marriage?

29:19.438 --> 29:21.930
A bottle of Scotch every night
before dinner.

29:22.024 --> 29:24.943
Your father has been sober 50 days now.

29:25.027 --> 29:28.864
We're very proud of that.

29:30.615 --> 29:36.246
Wow, Dad. I wonder what helped you
turn that corner?

29:37.623 --> 29:41.574
Think maybe it was a new lady friend?
You think maybe that's what it was?

29:41.668 --> 29:45.797
- I will not let you talk to me this...
- I will not let you sleep with my wife.

29:47.841 --> 29:51.710
Oh, Jack. Jack, I'm your father.

29:51.803 --> 29:54.295
Jack, please, just let it go.

30:19.247 --> 30:21.959
- Which way out?
- Don't do this, Jack.

30:22.042 --> 30:24.284
Don't... Don't...

30:36.765 --> 30:39.007
- No!
- Open the door.

30:39.101 --> 30:41.676
- I can't. I do that, we die.
- You're lying to me.

30:41.770 --> 30:43.480
- I'm not.
- Open the door!

30:43.563 --> 30:47.150
- I can't. I swear I can't.
- She's telling the truth, Jack.

30:50.445 --> 30:54.032
I swear to God, I will kill her.

30:55.367 --> 30:56.399
OK.

30:59.621 --> 31:04.668
Have her open the door
and she dies anyway. We all do.

31:11.591 --> 31:13.552
No!

31:40.162 --> 31:42.873
Jack! Over here!

32:02.934 --> 32:05.062
- The button!
- What?

32:05.145 --> 32:07.689
The yellow button! The button!

32:34.716 --> 32:36.624
Come here.

33:06.748 --> 33:08.792
<i>Warning.</i>

33:14.381 --> 33:16.842
Gotcha, Doc Brown!

33:18.427 --> 33:20.721
<i>Reward. Reward.</i>

33:26.893 --> 33:28.551
Come on.

33:34.026 --> 33:36.017
Unbelievable.

33:46.788 --> 33:48.947
Keep moving.

34:08.769 --> 34:12.189
Stick your hands out through the bars,
I'll take off your cuffs.

34:12.272 --> 34:15.306
Scratched you up pretty bad,
didn't they?

34:15.400 --> 34:20.030
- I'll bring you some antiseptic later.
- How about you bring me an ottoman?

34:20.113 --> 34:22.491
While you're at it,
I could use a blow-dry.

34:22.574 --> 34:27.871
Hey, you got yourself a fish biscuit.
How'd you do that?

34:27.955 --> 34:30.989
I figured out your complicated gizmos,
that's how.

34:31.083 --> 34:33.961
Only took the bears two hours.

34:35.504 --> 34:38.215
How many of 'em were there?

34:41.259 --> 34:43.136
You OK, Freckles?

34:47.015 --> 34:49.059
Yeah.

34:49.142 --> 34:52.312
- You?
- Just swell.

34:53.271 --> 34:56.692
I requested that cage, but whatever.

35:04.741 --> 35:07.942
Nice dress.

35:08.036 --> 35:10.664
They made me wear it.

35:19.256 --> 35:20.757
You hungry?

36:09.431 --> 36:12.966
It's an aquarium.

36:13.685 --> 36:16.720
- Excuse me?
- This thing's for what,

36:17.814 --> 36:21.735
- sharks?
- Dolphins, too.

36:29.952 --> 36:33.820
- We're underwater, aren't we?
- Yes.

36:34.831 --> 36:39.962
Is this one of their stations,
the Dharma Initiative?

36:40.045 --> 36:42.037
They called it the Hydra.

36:44.257 --> 36:46.666
So you people are just...

36:48.303 --> 36:50.879
...whatever's left over of them?

36:52.599 --> 36:55.602
Well, that was a long time ago.

36:58.271 --> 37:04.225
It doesn't matter who we were.

37:04.319 --> 37:07.489
It only matters who we are.

37:08.323 --> 37:10.951
We know exactly who you are,
Jack Shephard.

37:11.702 --> 37:14.110
You don't know anything about me.

37:14.830 --> 37:16.821
I know that you're a spinal surgeon

37:16.915 --> 37:20.335
based out of St. Sebastian's Hospital
in Los Angeles.

37:20.419 --> 37:22.045
I know you went to Columbia

37:22.129 --> 37:26.216
and you graduated med school
a year faster than anyone else.

37:26.300 --> 37:29.834
I know that you were married only once

37:29.928 --> 37:32.306
and that you contested the divorce.

37:34.266 --> 37:37.602
I know your father died in Sydney.

37:37.686 --> 37:42.983
I know this because
I have a copy of his autopsy report.

37:45.861 --> 37:47.852
How...

37:48.864 --> 37:51.356
- How did you get...
- We got it.

37:54.870 --> 37:57.414
What is that?

37:58.749 --> 38:03.712
This, Jack, is your life.

38:06.340 --> 38:08.665
Do you...?

38:08.759 --> 38:14.003
Is it just about me or is it about
my family, too? My... my friends?

38:14.097 --> 38:16.975
It's pretty much about everything.

38:19.227 --> 38:25.181
Do you know about my...
about my ex-wife?

38:25.275 --> 38:26.558
Sarah.

38:28.195 --> 38:33.075
Yes, Jack. We know all about her.

38:36.328 --> 38:39.247
What would you like to find out?

38:44.086 --> 38:45.879
Get ready for the lockdown.

38:45.963 --> 38:49.164
Shephard. Someone posted your bail.

39:04.106 --> 39:07.807
- How'd you...?
- Your dad told me you were here.

39:12.155 --> 39:14.564
I called you a cab.

39:14.658 --> 39:18.662
So, goodbye.

39:34.886 --> 39:37.921
- Sarah.
- What?

39:38.932 --> 39:40.434
Is that him?

39:40.517 --> 39:43.145
- What difference does it make?
- It just does.

39:43.228 --> 39:48.525
I wanna know. I need to know who he is.

39:48.608 --> 39:52.394
It doesn't matter who he is.
It just matters who you're not.

39:57.993 --> 40:03.915
Jack, your father,
when he called me,

40:03.999 --> 40:07.836
to help you,

40:07.919 --> 40:11.506
he was so drunk
I could hardly understand him.

40:19.514 --> 40:21.975
Look at the bright side.

40:23.560 --> 40:25.885
Now you have something to fix.

40:38.992 --> 40:40.786
<i>Jack.</i>

40:41.995 --> 40:46.792
Jack, what would you like to find out?

40:51.922 --> 40:53.913
Is she...

40:56.051 --> 40:58.178
Is she happy?

41:00.347 --> 41:05.175
Yes, Jack, she's very happy.

41:17.990 --> 41:21.357
Now, I'd like to bring you
some food and water.

41:21.451 --> 41:25.914
But this time I need to know
that you'll behave.

41:25.998 --> 41:28.490
Can I trust you, Jack?

41:35.340 --> 41:39.511
Put your back against the wall, please.

42:12.210 --> 42:14.588
Good work, Juliet.

42:17.215 --> 42:20.177
Thank you, Ben.
